---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import GrowthCalculator from '../../../components/GrowthCalculator.astro';
import SourceLinks from '../../../components/SourceLinks.astro';
import ToolHero from '../../../components/ToolHero.astro';
import NextSteps from '../../../components/NextSteps.astro';
import ToolExplainer from '../../../components/ToolExplainer.astro';
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebApplication',
  name: 'Trump Account Growth Calculator',
  applicationCategory: 'FinanceApplication',
  operatingSystem: 'Any web browser',
  isAccessibleForFree: true,
  description: 'Illustrates Trump Account contributions, hypothetical returns, fee impact, and balances across multiple scenarios.'
};
---
<BaseLayout title="Trump Account Growth Calculator" description="Model family and employer contributions, the $1,000 pilot amount, fees, and multiple hypothetical return scenarios." verifiedAt="2026-10-15">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
  <div class="shell"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'Home',href:'/'},{label:'Tools',href:'/tools/'},{label:'Growth calculator'}]} /></div>
  <ToolHero title="Trump Account growth calculator" description="Explore contributions, returns, and fees. An illustration—not a forecast." date="2026-10-15" dateLabel="Calculation version" />
  <div class="shell">
    <GrowthCalculator />
    <ToolExplainer name="Trump Account growth calculator"
      steps={[
        { title: 'Choose a contribution plan', text: 'Enter a family amount, monthly or yearly frequency, an assumed return, and a target age. Monthly deposits are modeled at month-end; yearly deposits at December 31.' },
        { title: 'Check the example assumptions', text: 'Open Dates & pilot amount to change the fictional birth and start dates. The pilot starts at No. Starting balances, employer deposits, and fees are available under Advanced assumptions.' },
        { title: 'Compare, then keep the assumptions', text: 'Update the projection, compare the return scenarios, and read the annual table. Print the report to retain the inputs and calculation version. A modeled balance is not a forecast.' }
      ]}
      features={[
        { title: 'Calendar-year checks', text: 'Scheduled deposits are checked in each modeled calendar year, including partial years. Earlier and outside deposits are not known.' },
        { title: 'Fees shown separately', text: 'Compare the same cash flows with and without the fund and account-fee assumptions.' },
        { title: 'Reproducible illustrations', text: 'The chart, annual table, and printable assumptions come from the same monthly model.' },
        { title: 'No account access', text: 'Inputs stay in this browser. No signup, account number, SSN, or connection to a financial provider is needed.' }
      ]}
      useCase="Use it to explore a household contribution idea, compare fee assumptions, or prepare questions for a trustee or adviser. It does not calculate tax bills, remaining legal contribution capacity, or a personalized investment recommendation."
      questions={[
        { title: 'Is the $1,000 pilot amount included by default?', text: 'No. Turning it on adds a starting-balance assumption at the projection start. It does not confirm eligibility, an election, receipt of money, or a government payment date.' },
        { title: 'Why can the contribution cutoff differ from the target date?', text: 'The model separates the statutory growth-period end from the selected projection target. A younger target can shorten the contribution schedule; a later target does not add post-growth-period IRA contributions. Both dates appear in the result.' },
        { title: 'How are partial calendar years handled?', text: 'The limit check adds the family and employer deposits actually scheduled in each calendar year. It does not assume twelve monthly deposits in a partial year or know what other contributors already deposited.' },
        { title: 'Are fees, taxes, and inflation all included?', text: 'The selected fund-expense and account-fee assumptions are included. Taxes, inflation, withdrawals, tracking error, market sequence, and partial months are not modeled. The result is a nominal, hypothetical illustration.' },
        { title: 'Why did the previous result disappear?', text: 'Changing an input hides the old result and disables printing until you update the projection. Blank numeric fields must be completed, including an explicit zero where appropriate.' },
        { title: 'Can I use this as a 529 calculator?', text: 'No. This tool uses the Trump Account model and contribution schedule. The account comparison and 529 guide explain other account types; this is not a 529 projection or a ranking of providers.' }
      ]}
    />
    <NextSteps heading="A balance is one part of the picture." links={[
      { title: 'Compare the account rules', description: 'Explore purpose, ownership, and withdrawal differences.', href: '/tools/child-savings-account-comparison/' },
      { title: 'Check contribution limits', description: 'Understand how family and employer amounts fit together.', href: '/contributions/trump-account-contribution-limits/' }
    ]} />
  </div>
  <section class="section tint">
    <div class="article-body shell">
      <h2>Calculation method</h2>
      <p>The model calculates the statutory growth-period end from the birth date: December 31 of the calendar year in which the child turns 17. It applies a monthly equivalent of the selected annual return, subtracts monthly equivalents of the fund-expense and account-fee assumptions, deposits monthly family contributions at month-end, and deposits annual family and employer contributions at December 31.</p>
      <p>The start date cannot precede July 4, 2026. The optional pilot amount is modeled at the projection start, not on a predicted government payment date. Changing an input hides the prior result until you calculate again; blank numeric fields must be completed, including an explicit zero where appropriate.</p>
      <p>Headline balances are rounded to whole dollars for readability. Report assumptions preserve the numeric precision used in the calculation, including small fee rates such as 0.004%, so the inputs can be reproduced.</p>
      <p>Limit checks sum the family and employer deposits actually scheduled in each calendar year, including partial years. They do not assess earlier or outside deposits, or future inflation-indexed limits. The modeled contribution cutoff may precede the statutory growth-period end when a younger target age is selected. The chart and annual table reconcile to the same month-end calculation.</p>
      <p>The “fee impact” compares the same cash flows with and without both fee assumptions. The 0.10% ceiling applies to the eligible investment fund; separate trustee or intermediary fees require their own analysis. Partial months, taxes, inflation, tracking error, market sequence, actual deposit timing, and withdrawals are not modeled.</p>
      <SourceLinks ids={['TREASURY-TD-10056','IRS-PROPOSED-INVESTMENTS-2026','IRS-REV-PROC-2026-25']} />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
